    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "At every dyadic e=2 exact-ratio boundary m=3h+2 with h>2, two square-class normalizations reduce each ordered scaling orbit to a triple (epsilon,x,a). Reciprocal linearization forces the locator below its endpoint, and the degree-(h+1) equation f_(h+1)=0 gives E_h^prim(m,p)<=2(m-1)(h+1)=2(m^2-1)/3.",
